# Cloudflare Pages applies these only when no static asset matches, so a
# PUBLISHED feed never reaches them. Most specific first.
# Record and corrections became one page. Both old paths are published, linked
# from a partner placement, and indexed, so they move rather than break.
/record/               /proof/                301
/record                /proof/                301
/corrections/          /proof/#corrections    301
/corrections           /proof/#corrections    301
# MEASURED, not assumed. Two shapes were tried against the live site and
# neither matched, so `/feed-not-found.json` is published and unreachable and a
# partner asking for a feed on an unpublished date gets the HTML 404 below,
# where the contract promises a JSON error body:
#
#   /archive/*/feed.json      splat in the middle of a path. Never matched.
#   /archive/:slug/feed.json  named placeholder. Also never matched.
#
# What DOES work here is a literal path with a 3xx (the four rules above are
# live and verified) and the trailing `/*` catch-all below. So on Pages this
# file cannot express "any feed path we did not publish".
#
# The remaining option is a Pages Function at functions/archive/[slug]/, which
# would work, and which would also sit in front of EVERY published feed
# including the ones partners actually read. That is a much larger surface to
# put a new failure mode on than the defect justifies, so it is a decision to
# take deliberately rather than a fix to slip in. Left broken and written down.
/*                         /404.html              404
